# PowerShell 5.1 + WPF

Windows PowerShell wraps cmdlet output in `[psobject]`. That wrapper makes .NET overloads throw **«Типы аргумента не совпадают»**.

```powershell
# BAD — New-Object wraps; @() then throws (PowerShell #27558)
$list = New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[object]
@($list)

# GOOD
$list = [System.Collections.Generic.List[object]]::new()
foreach ($item in $list) { }
```

Never call from PowerShell (ambiguous with WinForms, or PSObject-typed args):

- `$window.ShowDialog()`, `[Windows.Application]::Run($window)`, `[Dispatcher]::PushFrame($frame)`
- `[DockPanel]::SetDock($el, 'Left')` — use `StackPanel` or set attached properties in C#
- `[Windows.MessageBox]` / `[Windows.Application]` — always `System.Windows.MessageBox` / `System.Windows.Application`

Do:

- Create WPF objects with `::new()`, not `New-Object`, when they go into typed .NET APIs
- Show/hide windows via `[ZapretUiHost]::StartMainLoop()`, `ShowSettings()`, `HideSettings()` — do not assign void .NET methods to `$null` / `[void]`
- Set `Owner` only after the main window is visible (`AttachSettingsOwner`)
- Wrap `DispatcherTimer` ticks and `Loaded` in `try/catch` so one UI error does not tear down the message loop
